2. ARTWORK AND TEXT - Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
   (CC BY 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   Applies to the written documents (README.md), the screenshots in shots/ and
   the audio samples in audio/.
   Allophone names and numbering follow the General Instrument SP0256-AL2 for
   familiarity only; all sounds are newly synthesised. The letter-to-sound rules
   are based on the public-domain 1976 NRL report (Elovitz et al.).

This is original, clean-room work. It contains no Sinclair, Amstrad or other
ROM code, and no ROM image; it needs the OpticOS ROM
(https://github.com/brixham99/OpticOS). "ZX Spectrum" and "Sinclair" are used
only to name the machine and belong to their respective owners.
